WEBVTT

00:02:57.799 --> 00:03:00.218
and is focused on what I want from them.

00:03:00.777 --> 00:03:03.858
I'm telling them how to move
their body and when,

00:03:03.882 --> 00:03:06.102
regardless of their comfort or fear.

00:03:07.176 --> 00:03:11.329
This often results in terrified beginners
who never come back.

00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:14.891
Meanwhile, the way
I now talk to my students

00:03:14.915 --> 00:03:17.386
gives a lot more care to the person,

00:03:17.410 --> 00:03:19.769
ensuring they're fully informed,

00:03:19.793 --> 00:03:20.944
ready

00:03:20.968 --> 00:03:22.764
and part of the conversation.

00:03:23.610 --> 00:03:26.564
Adie Delaney: How do you feel about it?
Student: Really good.

00:03:26.588 --> 00:03:29.427
AD: I feel like you could probably do it.
Want to have a go?

00:03:29.451 --> 00:03:31.196
Student: OK.
AD: That's it, yes.